      "solution": "n = int(input())\nres = []\nfor _ in range(n):\n    parts = input().split()\n    k = int(parts[0])\n    ch = parts[1]\n    res.append(ch * k)\nprint(\"\".join(res))\n",
      "statement": "You are given a run-length encoded sequence of [[N]] elements.\n\nEach element consists of an integer repetition [[count]] and a single character [[char]].\n\nYour task is to decompress the sequence by repeating each [[char]] exactly [[count]] times, and output the reconstructed string.",
