    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">You are given a run-length encoded sequence of <var>N</var> elements.<br><br>Each element consists of an integer repetition <var>count</var> and a single character <var>char</var>.<br><br>Your task is to decompress the sequence by repeating each <var>char</var> exactly <var>count</var> times, and output the reconstructed string.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\">Line 1: An integer <var>N</var> representing the number of compressed chunks.<br>Next <var>N</var> lines: An integer <var>count</var> and a character <var>char</var>, separated by a space.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\">A single line containing the fully decompressed string.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; <var>N</var> &le; 100<br>1 &le; <var>count</var> &le; 100<br><var>char</var> is a printable non-whitespace ASCII character.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">3\n3 A\n2 B\n4 C</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">AAABBCCCC</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
